WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:01.713
(dial tone)

00:00:01.713 --> 00:00:02.835
(dialing)

00:00:02.835 --> 00:00:04.003
(upbeat music)
- You've got ... you've got ..

00:00:04.003 --> 00:00:05.664
You've got mail!

00:00:05.664 --> 00:00:06.497
You've got ... you've got ...

00:00:06.497 --> 00:00:07.847
You've got mail!

00:00:07.847 --> 00:00:08.680
Goodbye!

00:00:08.680 --> 00:00:11.070
- To all of you who thought
AOL was voiced by a computer,

00:00:11.070 --> 00:00:13.480
now let's set the record straight.

00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:15.334
I recorded those phrases.

00:00:15.334 --> 00:00:16.462
Welcome (dinging).

00:00:16.462 --> 00:00:17.587
You've got mail (dinging).

00:00:17.587 --> 00:00:18.808
File's done (dinging)

00:00:18.808 --> 00:00:20.324
Goodbye (beeping)

00:00:20.324 --> 00:00:22.178
My name is Elwood Edwards

00:00:22.178 --> 00:00:25.055
And I'm the voice of You've Got Mail.

00:00:25.055 --> 00:00:28.638
In 1989, my wife was
a customer service rep

00:00:30.726 --> 00:00:34.997
for the company that was about
to become American Online.

00:00:34.997 --> 00:00:37.506
She heard Steve Case talking
to some of the programmers

00:00:37.506 --> 00:00:41.686
about how fun it would be to
add a voice to the software.

00:00:41.686 --> 00:00:43.198
I'd been an announcer throughout

00:00:43.198 --> 00:00:45.708
my entire broadcasting career

00:00:45.708 --> 00:00:47.625
and she volunteered me.

00:00:48.716 --> 00:00:51.220
I scribbled those phrases
on a piece of paper

00:00:51.220 --> 00:00:53.166
and, like I say on the
cassette deck, I recorded

00:00:53.166 --> 00:00:57.252
the welcome, you've got
mail, files done, goodbye.

00:00:57.252 --> 00:00:58.085
(dinging)

00:00:58.085 --> 00:01:01.537
It started off as a test just
to see if it would catch on

00:01:01.537 --> 00:01:05.605
and, lo and behold, in the
mid-90's it had really caught on

00:01:05.605 --> 00:01:08.558
and at one point they
said my voice was heard

00:01:08.558 --> 00:01:11.308
more than 35 million times a day.

00:01:12.459 --> 00:01:14.311
(dialing)
But the problem was,

00:01:14.311 --> 00:01:16.146
I was typecast.

00:01:16.146 --> 00:01:19.786
The one thing I did do was
a voice for The Simpsons.

00:01:19.786 --> 00:01:21.513
- You've got leprosy.

00:01:21.513 --> 00:01:22.715
- [Both] Leprosy!

00:01:22.715 --> 00:01:24.226
- Goodbye.

00:01:24.226 --> 00:01:27.292
- Being associated with
AOL has been gratifying.

00:01:27.292 --> 00:01:29.792
Even today, you go on AOL.com.

00:01:30.985 --> 00:01:32.246
I greet you.

00:01:32.246 --> 00:01:34.728
I greet myself (laughs).

00:01:34.728 --> 00:01:38.145
(relaxing music)

